  "id": "DrugBank_DB00997 - MONDO_18172",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin, a well-known anthracycline chemotherapy agent, appears to have a potential role in the treatment of Malignant Sex Cord Stromal Tumor Of Ovary through a series of indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Doxorubicin is associated with Ovarian Mucinous Adenocarcinoma and Ovarian Clear Cell Adenocarcinoma, both of which are linked to other drugs such as cisplatin and carboplatin, which in turn are indicated for Malignant Sex Cord Stromal Tumor Of Ovary. This implies a possible mechanism of action where Doxorubicin may exert antitumor effects through similar pathways as these other drugs, potentially by targeting cancer cells through DNA damage or other cellular processes. The presence of multiple indirect pathways, each involving Doxorubicin in a different context, suggests that the drug may have a broad therapeutic profile in the treatment of ovarian tumors, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Doxorubicin to be repurposed in the treatment of this rare and aggressive malignancy.",
